			"notes": "PermaClicker 2.0.0 moves to TurtleLib 2.0.0 and the MIT license, makes Mining mode safer around mobs and players, and fixes the toggle key and the update notice.\n\n# Compatibility\n\n- **TurtleLib 2.0.0:** PermaClicker now requires TurtleLib 2.0.0 or newer; update both mods together.\n- **NeoForge:** Requires NeoForge 26.3.0.76 or newer, the first stable NeoForge release for Minecraft 26.3.\n\n# Improvements\n\n- **Translated status:** The action-bar status now appears in your game language.\n- **Settings file:** A damaged settings file is kept as `permaclicker.json.broken` instead of being overwritten, and saving can no longer leave an empty file.\n\n# Fixes\n\n- **Mining mode:** Mobs, animals and players that step in front of the block are no longer hit, and mining stops as soon as you look away from the block.\n- **Toggle key:** `F7` no longer ignores a press after a menu was open, and the misleading \"toggle key was reset\" message is gone.\n- **Attack key:** PermaClicker now uses your own attack key binding instead of the default one.\n- **Dedicated servers:** PermaClicker no longer stops a NeoForge server from starting when it is installed there by mistake; the server now skips it.\n- **Update notice:** The update check works again, only reports versions for your loader and Minecraft version, and its links open the release directly.\n- **NeoForge warning:** The \"deprecated logoFile\" warning no longer appears in the NeoForge log.\n\n# Other\n\n- **Update privacy:** The README and wiki now list which services the update check asks and what they receive.\n- **Mod details:** Updated description, icon and links in Mod Menu and the NeoForge mod list.\n- **MIT license:** PermaClicker is now licensed under MIT (previously Apache-2.0).\n- **Build from source:** The repository now builds on its own, without the development workspace.\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/hrobasti/permaclicker-mod/compare/1.4.0...2.0.0"
		},
